WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:01.773
Module 8A.

00:02.123 --> 00:05.466
Firm governance: building the AI governance programme.

00:05.816 --> 00:08.200
This module is for firm leadership and the

00:08.200 --> 00:10.286
person accountable for AI at the firm.

00:10.636 --> 00:15.550
It sets out the components of a written AI governance programme that meets

00:15.550 --> 00:20.087
professional obligations and stands up to scrutiny from clients, courts and insurers.

00:21.837 --> 00:26.264
By the end of this module you will be able to: set

00:26.264 --> 00:30.691
up the AI Governance Lead role and accountability; write an AI Use

00:30.691 --> 00:35.118
Policy with an approved-tool register; run vendor due diligence for high-materiality tools;

00:35.118 --> 00:38.439
control agentic AI and attest that the programme operates.

00:40.189 --> 00:43.463
A credible AI governance programme has ten components.

00:43.813 --> 00:48.735
A named AI Governance Lead: a partner or senior lawyer with real authority.

00:49.085 --> 00:54.171
A written AI Use Policy setting out approved, restricted and prohibited uses.

00:54.521 --> 00:57.580
A tool register listing every AI tool, what it may

00:57.580 --> 01:00.639
be used for, and what data may go into it.

01:00.989 --> 01:05.203
A review protocol built on the tiers and five checks from module five.

01:05.553 --> 01:09.176
Logging and retention of prompts, outputs and versions.

01:09.526 --> 01:12.266
Training on joining and annually, with records.

01:12.616 --> 01:15.112
An approval gate for agentic AI.

01:15.462 --> 01:16.913
Vendor due diligence.

01:17.263 --> 01:20.398
A procedure for court rules and client disclosure.

01:20.748 --> 01:22.466
And an incident process.

01:22.816 --> 01:24.871
Let's look at the most important ones.

01:26.621 --> 01:28.780
Start with the AI Governance Lead.

01:29.130 --> 01:32.160
This should be a partner or senior lawyer, formally

01:32.160 --> 01:34.854
appointed by the managing partner or governing body.

01:35.204 --> 01:39.639
The role carries authority to approve tools, enforce the policy, receive incident reports

01:39.639 --> 01:44.074
and sign an annual attestation that the programme is in place and working.

01:44.424 --> 01:48.174
The Lead is usually supported by an AI champion in IT

01:48.174 --> 01:51.924
or knowledge management and, in larger firms, a small AI committee.

01:52.274 --> 01:56.145
The whole programme should be reviewed and re-approved at least once a

01:56.145 --> 01:59.693
year, and any change of Lead should be documented and communicated.

02:01.443 --> 02:04.792
The AI Use Policy should state which tools are

02:04.792 --> 02:08.142
approved, for which tasks, and which uses are prohibited.

02:08.492 --> 02:11.916
That includes using consumer-grade tools for client work

02:11.916 --> 02:14.912
unless the Governance Lead specifically approves it.

02:15.262 --> 02:19.076
The policy is backed by a tool register, with a row

02:19.076 --> 02:22.890
for every AI tool, including AI features embedded in existing software.

02:23.240 --> 02:28.329
Record the tool and vendor, the plan and its data terms, approved and

02:28.329 --> 02:33.418
prohibited tasks, the decision materiality, meaning how directly the output can shape client

02:33.418 --> 02:38.507
advice, whether logging is enabled and exportable, and who approved it and when.

02:38.857 --> 02:41.727
Every person who uses AI in client work should

02:41.727 --> 02:44.279
receive the policy and acknowledge it in writing.

02:46.029 --> 02:51.404
For every tool with high decision materiality, run vendor due diligence before approval.

02:51.754 --> 02:57.629
Read the terms on data use, retention, confidentiality, security and data location.

02:57.979 --> 03:04.027
Find the liability position: caps, exclusions, indemnities and any waiver of claims.

03:04.377 --> 03:07.506
Most vendor terms cap the vendor's liability sharply, which

03:07.506 --> 03:10.287
means the firm carries most of the risk.

03:10.637 --> 03:14.039
Note any claim-notice period, because some contracts require you to

03:14.039 --> 03:17.440
notify the vendor of an incident within a short window.

03:17.790 --> 03:20.948
And keep a dated copy of the terms that were in

03:20.948 --> 03:24.106
force when the tool was approved and used, because terms change.

03:25.856 --> 03:28.085
Three more controls complete the programme.

03:28.435 --> 03:30.711
First, the agentic approval gate.

03:31.061 --> 03:35.730
Configure any agent so that it cannot file, serve, send, sign, commit,

03:35.730 --> 03:40.399
disclose, withdraw or delete without prior approval by a reviewing lawyer, and

03:40.399 --> 03:44.679
name a person who can halt or reverse what it does.

03:45.029 --> 03:46.504
Second, monitoring.

03:46.854 --> 03:51.599
Track training completion, errors caught at review, near-misses, policy breaches and spot-audit

03:51.599 --> 03:56.344
results, and run a quarterly spot audit that re-checks a sample of

03:56.344 --> 04:00.298
AI-assisted work to confirm the reviews and records are real.

04:00.648 --> 04:02.622
Third, annual attestation.

04:02.972 --> 04:07.488
The Governance Lead confirms in writing that the programme is in place and operating.

04:07.838 --> 04:12.575
Clients, courts and insurers increasingly ask for exactly this evidence.

04:14.325 --> 04:15.939
Let's recap the key points.

04:16.289 --> 04:18.866
Appoint a Governance Lead with real authority.

04:19.216 --> 04:23.872
Approved-tool register plus written policy, acknowledged by every user.

04:24.221 --> 04:28.598
Vendor diligence for high-materiality tools; keep dated terms.

04:28.948 --> 04:33.024
Gate agentic AI; audit quarterly; attest annually.

04:34.774 --> 04:35.760
Knowledge check.

04:36.110 --> 04:40.894
An associate starts using a new AI feature inside the firm's document software.

04:41.244 --> 04:42.579
What should happen first?

04:42.929 --> 04:46.969
Option A: Nothing; it's part of software already approved.

04:47.319 --> 04:50.204
Option B: It is assessed and added to the

04:50.204 --> 04:53.089
tool register by the Governance Lead before client use.

04:53.439 --> 04:57.630
Option C: The associate tells IT after the matter closes.

04:57.980 --> 05:00.860
Take a moment to decide before the answer appears.

05:06.610 --> 05:08.130
The answer is option B.

05:08.480 --> 05:10.965
Embedded AI features are AI tools.

05:11.315 --> 05:15.796
They need assessment, approved tasks and data rules before client use.
